{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game","id":1075873,"title":"\u200bCritical Thoughts on the Potential in a 5th Edition of the Game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-10T07:26:33-07:00","id":1075873,"title":"\u200bCritical Thoughts on the Potential in a 5th Edition of the Game.","content":"In another thread I was compelled into a confrontation over the nature of the ST System and difficulties in the current market. My honorable opposition is not an intuitor primary, and the difference in our posits has more to do with the division between the analysis of sensual perception and the analysis of conceptual perception. These are both valid approaches, each with their own inherent pros and cons.<br /> <br /> A problem for all Fantasy Entertainment, is the combination of treacherous bubble and economic downturn. Real wealth incomes in the US, and the majority of the Western World, have been in decline since the economic policy shifts of the 1980's. While the numbers have increased, the value of those numbers has decreased. Because reality has been more difficult, the celebration of reality has been less - that is people prefer to buy fantasy when the reality sucks. Hence, the mass support for superhero films, an entire network devoted to fantasy (CW), the history channel focussing on myth rather than modern events, etc. It was the same during the 80's when artists who sold fantasy illustration or subjects of a by-gone golden age made money hand over fists while those who sold portraits, still life, and landscapes struggled. So, while the current economic climate of the past three decades supports the sales of fantasy entertainment, to include RPGs and video RPGs, that market share has been the facade of austere economic pressures where the bulk of society is receiving less and less in real world assets. From the distant vantage, the move from mass published HB rules to digital publishing is just another leaf floating along the dwindling stream of resources supporting the general public. Those with a more myopic vantage point will not see this because they stand amidst the trees.<br /> <br /> Following this stream of events, the directing of budgetary support de-emphasized (conceptually abandoned) the Classic World of Darkness. This was an event that did not sit well with those of us who were not done with what that avenue had to offer. Further, there were many of us who simply felt the way it ended was petite for an apocalypse - like a small lump of bread pudding to cap off a 12 course meal of beautifully crafted gourmet presentations. A truly apocalyptic ending would have restored the Bringer of Harmony or devoured the Wild leaving the Weaver nothing to weave but the broken remains of what could have been. The new materials moved toward a more universal concept of play, and abandoned an intentional meta for an unintended one implied by the materials of the game.<br /> <br /> Some consider the evolution of the games in such short a time to be a simple response to market pressures. These would be short term market concerns. When the Japanese began defeating the American Auto industry it was because they were making decisions based on generations of impact rather than merely responding to short term market influences. A more Jungian approach, one that responds to the universality of the soul, is already inherent in the Story Teller System. However, it seems to be treated as an occasional daliance between flirtatious friends rather than capitalized upon for the expansive possibilities it entails.<br /> <br /> One point of disagreement is whether or not the Story Teller System is or is meant to be more universal in its approach. Another is whether it encourages the suspension of disbelief. That the rules promote the deliberate deferrence to the suspension of disbelief over game mechanics is and of itself is a mechanic in the rules encouraging the suspension of disbelief. This is, as I view it, also a problem for marketing against the larger more familiar and less imagination supporting game systems.<br /> <br /> Where other systems, such as Shadowrun, AD&amp;D, etc. have dominated the market it is in large part because they have a massive amount of edutainment support in the video gaming industry. Seven year olds will learn the basic ability scores, hp system, leveling up, etc. of less imaginative gaming systems from the various games they play. In many ways, AD&amp;D is just a video game on paper where mass accumulation of points, like mass accumulation of wealth, is the only goal and the expansion of the mind, the feeding of the soul, is utterly neglected. &quot;Give me four years to teach the children and the seed I have sown will never be uprooted,&quot; said Lenin. Well, the opposing team gets many more than that and it took 3/4s of a century to undo what Lenin did. So, while it remains true that familiarity may breed contempt, it is more true that familiarity embraces convenience. The greatest boon to the ST system would be a base game which can be easily promoted at the juvenile level both in Pen and Paper and in Video.<br /> <br /> From an intuitive point of view all of the games published by White Wolf and Onyx Path are merely variations on a theme. All of them can be re-interpreted into a singular gaming action. Whether it is from WoD, CoD, Exalted, Scion, or Trinity - the conceptual material is adaptable across the games because it is born out of a consistent theme of struggle and similar mechanics. They are not however sensually identical, which makes them difficult to plug and play with one another without hours of conversion for each. So, while the mechanics of these systems are universally applicable, they are not conveniently interactive. The Translation Guides deliver a base support for abandoning one game series for the other. They demonstrate how to transition characters. They fail to transition things like Axis Mundi, to make the metas of each system playable in the other.<br /> <br /> This latter was a problem for me in playing the initial games. The constantly changing mechanics within the same system made adapting them into the same world difficult. The worst two for this were Wraith and Changeling. The structure of wraith made it virtually impossible to interact with the Skinlands where all the other games took place. The system of powers for Changelings simply came across as an unreliable game of table craps. One of the reasons I collected the books, but never played or even tried to play a Changeling. In every aspect of mechanics the CoD was an improvement for both play and for interaction between the various games.<br /> <br /> The only thing that the system has ever really lacked for universality of play is a system of rules for tech level. Tables of Equipment and pricing for different eras: Stone Age, Bronze Age, Iron Age, Renaissance, Enlightenment, Industrial Age, Computer Age, Interplanetary Age, Interstellar Age, Intergalactic Age, and potentially a Transdimensional Age. Some of this is adaptable from the different publications by Onyx Path. Some of it has not been deliberately explored.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of the early games was the brilliance of its inculcation of the classical mind into the ambiance of the game at the very warp and weft of it. Intentionally or unintentionally the game congealed the roiling thoughts of humanities best thinkers into an expression of its variant philosophical approaches, its most important ethical dilemmas, and the epic journey of the flawed hero. Each of the five base games explored a specific moral dilemma for humanity. In vampire the question was begged: If we are evil by the nature of what we are, how do we strive to be good and remain sane? In werewolf: How do we deal with the frustration of being the only one's who can see what is really going on in a world destroying itself? In mage: How do we find a way for utterly disparate paradigms to exist peacefully side by side off of the same limited resources? In Wraith: If we are the victims of an extreme trauma how do we over come the shadows on our soul it leaves behind and transcend to the better? And in Changeling: How do we balance the curious playful adventurous side of our soul with the mundane pragmatic risk-averse necessities of social life? Those questions became less conspicuous in CoD than they were in WoD. And this made the journey of the flawed hero less observable. There was no longer a path directing the journey from where we find the hero of our story and the character development they must inevitably achieve or tragically fail to make.<br /> <br /> Assuming there will be a 5th Edition game, it would be my hope that it would address these concerns.<br /> 1) Create a marketable version for a juvenile game which captures a market share of minds early on.<br /> 2) Establish a better presence in the Video gaming industry.<br /> 3) Use a base character sheet for mundanes as the source for a sequentially written table of contents which explains all basic game mechanics. (e.g. use of Attributes, Abilities/Skills, Backgrounds/Conditions, Merits, Flaws, Virtue/Integrity, Will Power, Health, etc.) This would be a down and dirty pocket reference for quick start introduction.<br /> 4) Prepare a base template system that allows the easy incorporation of all previously published game materials. These could be published separately, in installments, covering different aspects which have previously been separate games. Thus becoming a vampire, discovering one is a were-X, dying with some fetter that prevents one from truly moving on, etc. becomes an addition or development of the base character.<br /> 5) Establish technology based equipment guides supporting expansive play possibilities.<br /> 6) Campaign materials which do not change or add to the mechanics, but which provide support for master plots in various milieus: Past, Present, Future, and on the other side of the looking glass. As always, dazzle us with the art, &quot;the real relation, the underlying theme&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 04-10-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:43:13-07:00","id":1075879,"title":"","content":"Warp and weft, not warp and woof. It's a fiber arts term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:08:14-07:00","id":1075919,"title":"","content":"Having read a number of your posts on this topic... I'm still kind of confused about what exactly you want. You complain about mechanics changing between editions, yet you assert that you prefer CofD mechanics to WoD mechanics. You reject the idea that innovation and advancement occurs over time in game design, but how would the mechanics you prefer have come into existence without the process of change and experimentation? You claim to want a series of changes to the mechanics and structure of the games that makes it conform more closely to your expectations, yet you also say you want &quot;Campaign materials which do not change or add to the mechanics.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:23:05-07:00","id":1075922,"title":"","content":"I believe some of his suggestion, or 'critical thoughts,' are about making World of Darkness a bit more like Chronicles. For instance having the base mortal template that can then be changed into a monster for the other games. Though I think with what World of Darkness games are meant to be like, according to the guy in charge, that's not likely to happen at all. In these games, it seems like the human experience is meant to be out of reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:50:38-07:00","id":1076008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1075922#post1075922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe some of his suggestion, or 'critical thoughts,' are about making World of Darkness a bit more like Chronicles. For instance having the base mortal template that can then be changed into a monster for the other games. Though I think with what World of Darkness games are meant to be like, according to the guy in charge, that's not likely to happen at all. In these games, it seems like the human experience is meant to be out of reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about that. How did you got this impression?<br /> <br /> If anything, I expect a more unified system between the games, which probably means some kind of &quot;base template&quot;, which likely means mortals. That and their plans to &quot;make humans more important&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:16:52-07:00","id":1076030,"title":"","content":"The problem for the gaming industry is not the change in editions, the majority of gaming companies wait five to ten years before they come out with a new edition (if not longer), it is the change in consumer preferences caused by the isolating effect of the internet. It is much easier to get people to fork over money for gaming products when they have people who they physically know who will be willing to play with them. In my own experience, I am usually the ST and the first buyer of the groups that I am part of and, when I run a game, my players usually buy their own copies of the books after the first game. <br /> <br /> One problem that a number of people I know have is that the gaming population is aging and the majority of people have the books that they need. In my own case, I have over three hundred physical books from over a dozen different systems (cWoD, Scion, Exalted, GURPS, AFMBE, L5R, Heroes, Pathfinder, Eclipse Phase, BESM, Conan, Feng Shui, Savage Worlds, Mutants and Masterminds, etc), and that is what is just what is in my living room. I am getting to the point where I really start wondering if I need any more physical books, but I buy them out of loyalty to the companies that I like. There are plenty of people though who just want the books from one or two systems and really do not want or need to expand beyond their current collection unless they join a physical game where the ST is running an unfamiliar system (I doubt that many people join internet games where people are using unfamiliar systems).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:06:50-07:00","id":1076094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1075919#post1075919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read a number of your posts on this topic... I'm still kind of confused about what exactly you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, analitical observation does not necessarily mean conclusion. Sometimes, it is merely a statement of observation. That is not necessarily a complaint; and this doesn't mean that I haven't had complaints - only that everything perceived as such may not have been one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You complain about mechanics changing between editions, yet you assert that you prefer CofD mechanics to WoD mechanics. </div> </div> </div>That hasn't actually been the complaint. The complaint has been that such changes are used to obliterate the value of all the collected materials. None of my 1st Ed AD&amp;D was compatible with 2nd Ed. The difference in ST editions was not so extreme, but the result has been similar. Wanting to continue the Classic Meta with the new rule set was not supported functionally. The Marauders, Nefandi, Fomori, Malfeans, Spectres, Banes, Totems, etc. of the Classic Meta have no support in the unintended meta of the CoD system. I have been collecting CoD materials, which are much better at the way they handle mundanes. I have most of those books. I like the attendent God Machine materials, but not the God Machine Meta. I want the classic meta, which is in nature both more dynamic and more expressive of the human epic - especially since epic and universal forces are more easily reskinned. What is Brahma/Visnu/Shiva, Clotho/Lachesis/Atropos, al-Uzza/al-Lat/Manat, and the 10,000 times 10,000 other variations of Trimurti but refracted shadows cast by the Wyld/Weaver/Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You reject the idea that innovation and advancement occurs over time in game design, but how would the mechanics you prefer have come into existence without the process of change and experimentation? </div> </div> </div>I didn't reject that innovation and advancement occur. I questioned the destruction of the value of the previous materials. If I wish to convert the Tomb of Horrors from AD&amp;D 1.0 to Pathfinder - everything has a level rating, a difficulty rating, a direct correlation to a named spell, a named monster, a listing in the equipment tables, etc. I could do this in a day or so without much interuption. If I wish to convert the Keep on the Borderlands to Pathfinder - the materials transfer over by level, item name, monster name, etc. and can be formatted by challenge rating. WoD to CoD lacks that correlation. They were made separate games and the result is either play the new one and lose the value of everything you already had or play the old one and ignore the new materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You claim to want a series of changes to the mechanics and structure of the games that makes it conform more closely to your expectations, yet you also say you want &quot;Campaign materials which do not change or add to the mechanics.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I suggested preping the next incarntion of the system to last for generations. To make decisions and place them into a simpler book of mechanics, much like the first Traveller had a book for explanation and book of charts, tables, and mechanics. Maybe even make the mechanics book a 3-Ring Binder with topics listed by section rather than by page number, like a legal reference. Then the players can purchase an update for a few dollars and swap it for the section that has been repealed and replaced. Move the older one to a reserve book. Streamline the sytem mechanics so that rules changes are either completely optional or do not invalidate existing materials.<br /> <br /> Campaign materials would focus on ambiance, not mechanics. Therefore they would not change or add to the mechanics of play. Picking up a campaign product would provide a list of characters and items to detail, but would not specify the system to use. Better yet, templates in the different systems which would plug and play. Pull out the Methuselah Toreador Template and tag on the name Helena and her path and then Methuselah Brujah Template and write in Meneleus on the name line and his path. Or identify them as a Daeva Invictus and Gangrel Carthian - and indicate which premade template to use. Perhaps list a suggested tweak or two, but: Make it so the single parent of 3, working two part time jobs and running a game with their teenagers, can plug and play regardless of the mechanics they choose to enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":".  clarity 04-10-2017, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:07:34-07:00","id":1076095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076030#post1076030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is much easier to get people to fork over money for gaming products when they have people who they physically know who will be willing to play with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this analysis as probable in close to all circumstances. The community where I live now is 325 people and 20 miles from the nearest Walmart in any direction. The people I game with are on-line. The retail outlet in the area, which hosts nightly gaming sessions, is near a college - but I have no way of getting to it. My main source for almost all purchases is now mail order via the internet. As the internet sales format increases I expect retailing will continue to decrease, with produce outlets carrying non-perishables as a matter of convenience rather than markets carrying the wider variety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One problem that a number of people I know have is that the gaming population is aging and the majority of people have the books that they need. </div> </div> </div>That is where solidifying a system that will change less while generating materials that have a family appeal would be beneficial. I have sat at a table with multi-generation members of the same household playing. I occasionally video game with a family that has four generations of gamers, a single family, as the center of their guild. This changing dynamic may not yet be the norm, but it is one that is increasing. I know some men in construction that maintain MMORPG accounts so they can play with their kids on a daily basis when they are away on a job for 3 months at a time. So, what is wrong with preparing for and appealing to a market that is multi-generational and family possible - if not even family probable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 04-10-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:46:10-07:00","id":1076203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076094#post1076094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't reject that innovation and advancement occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that in another thread when it was suggested that mechanics changed over time because of the integration of new design concepts, you responded<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, there are no new concepts. Nihil nova sub soli. It is all merely a Hero with a Thousand Faces. The birth of each child is the invasion of a new barbarian to be civilized. Ex barbariae e duc eos. The perception you identify is the limited experience of the immature. Packaging individuated concepts, like writing different series of novels, does not require an end to the system. </div> </div> </div>which would seem to suggest a rejection of that premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I questioned the destruction of the value of the previous materials. </div> </div> </div>You keep coming back to this idea and I don't understand it. In what respect is their value destroyed? I didn't start playing D&amp;D until 2000, but when I did a group of brand new players used a combination of 1st and 2nd AD&amp;D edition books. They worked just fine. They worked just fine together, even. If a bunch of middle schoolers can hack that I fail to see how a grown ass adult can't make something work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The complaint has been that such changes are used to obliterate the value of all the collected materials. None of my 1st Ed AD&amp;D was compatible with 2nd Ed. The difference in ST editions was not so extreme, but the result has been similar. </div> </div> </div>Again, failing to see how the value has been &quot;obliterated&quot; nor how the changes are &quot;used&quot; in that way. Your comment about the relative compatibility/incompatibility of the systems is contradicted later in the exact same post when you say<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I wish to convert the Tomb of Horrors from AD&amp;D 1.0 to Pathfinder - everything has a level rating, a difficulty rating, a direct correlation to a named spell, a named monster, a listing in the equipment tables, etc. I could do this in a day or so without much interuption. If I wish to convert the Keep on the Borderlands to Pathfinder - the materials transfer over by level, item name, monster name, etc. and can be formatted by challenge rating. WoD to CoD lacks that correlation. They were made separate games and the result is either play the new one and lose the value of everything you already had or play the old one and ignore the new materials. </div> </div> </div>There's a heck of a lot more distance between AD&amp;D 1st edition and Pathfinder than there is between AD&amp;D 1st and 2nd. You say that the difference between WoD and CofD is not even as vast as that, and yet you then claim that they're irreconcilable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suggested preping the next incarntion of the system to last for generations. To make decisions and place them into a simpler book of mechanics, much like the first Traveller had a book for explanation and book of charts, tables, and mechanics. Maybe even make the mechanics book a 3-Ring Binder with topics listed by section rather than by page number, like a legal reference. Then the players can purchase an update for a few dollars and swap it for the section that has been repealed and replaced. Move the older one to a reserve book. Streamline the sytem mechanics so that rules changes are either completely optional or do not invalidate existing materials. </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is actually fairly close to the emerging design philosophy of 5th edition D&amp;D. A reaction against supplement glut, a focus on core mechanics that are expanded and updated piecemeal via free material available online. I'd recommend checking it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Campaign materials would focus on ambiance, not mechanics. Therefore they would not change or add to the mechanics of play. Picking up a campaign product would provide a list of characters and items to detail, but would not specify the system to use. Better yet, templates in the different systems which would plug and play. Pull out the Methuselah Toreador Template and tag on the name Helena and her path and then Methuselah Brujah Template and write in Meneleus on the name line and his path. Or identify them as a Daeva Invictus and Gangrel Carthian - and indicate which premade template to use. Perhaps list a suggested tweak or two, but: Make it so the single parent of 3, working two part time jobs and running a game with their teenagers, can plug and play regardless of the mechanics they choose to enjoy. </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately supplements that are all fluff and no crunch tend not to sell very well. Gamers gonna game. I certainly understand the desire to make plug and play easier for people who don't have a lot of time for game prep or homebrew. I think that's a big reason why adventure modules seem to be doing well lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:01:23-07:00","id":1076237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076203#post1076203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly understand the desire to make plug and play easier for people who don't have a lot of time for game prep or homebrew. I think that's a big reason why adventure modules seem to be doing well lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, WotC seem to be under the impression that more adventure modules are needed since that's been the bulk of their D&amp;D5e releases after the core three rulebooks.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I don't see a whole lot of adventure modules being put out by OPP for all of their releases. WoD20 included.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> And in regards to Tomb of Horrors...funnily enough the &quot;Tales of the Yawning Portal&quot; book recently was released. And that book was all about updating 5 classic D&amp;D modules to 5e. One of them being Tomb or Horrors.<br /> <br /> Plus, every single edition of D&amp;D there always seem to be some update to Tomb of Horrors released at some point for each new edition. I know 3-3.5 had one. 4e had one. And now 5e has one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:38:09-07:00","id":1076316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076203#post1076203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that in another thread when it was suggested that mechanics changed over time because of the integration of new design concepts, you responded<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076095#post1076095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, there are no new concepts. Nihil nova sub soli. It is all merely a Hero with a Thousand Faces. The birth of each child is the invasion of a new barbarian to be civilized. Ex barbariae e duc eos. The perception you identify is the limited experience of the immature. Packaging individuated concepts, like writing different series of novels, does not require an end to the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>which would seem to suggest a rejection of that premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Context. The person to whom I responded had just described the gaming community as a collection of seemingly flighty skittering birds jumping from feeder to feeder convinced that just over there the seeds will be different. In the hand a blade cast in bronze and a blade cast in steel may seem very different, but it is still only a blade. Exploring the human condition by acting out morality plays has existed since the ritual telling of the Ramayana began in the Treta Yuga. Rolling dice as a form of gaming has existed since before 3,000 BCE using hexahedrons made from sheep bones. Tetrahedrons going back before 2,600 BCE were used in games which re-enacted the battle between the imposed order of the gods against the primordial chaos from which the world was made in which the journey of man from life to death is fraught with obstacles, traps, and fortunes which propel us quickly along the path. Every video game is just an elaborately decorated version of Pong. <div align=\"center\">Nihil nova sub soli. Ex barbariae e duc eos.<br /> Nothing new under the Sun. From Barbarism to lead them out.</div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In what respect is their value destroyed? </div> </div> </div>For a collector those hard copies that have never been opened may have some value. For gaming, the meta was made incompatible with the new supposedly meta-free set of rules which were never meta-free. Werewolf is specifically antithetical to the original meta.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a bunch of middle-schoolers can hack that I fail to see how a grown ass adult can't make something work. </div> </div> </div>When I was a child they created child proof caps. My father would take me to the art classes he taught in continuing education. One night when the law required all things that might be poisonous in some way to have child proof caps, his students \u2013 mostly elderly people with arthritis, could not open their oil paints. Neither of course could my father, since they were child proof and he was an adult. So he handed it too me to open, and I did. The lady said, &quot;My how smart you are to be able to do this.&quot; To which I replied, &quot;Not really. It's just that children have all the time in the world to work on something and adults have too many things to do.&quot; Perhaps if you had been busy working in a coal mine or operating an automated loom like some urchin in the late 1800's you would have a better perspective of how our children may indulge themselves when not faced with the frivolous pursuits of paying bills, repairing the home, maintaining the car, buying and preparing food, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, failing to see how the value has been &quot;obliterated&quot; nor how the changes are &quot;used&quot; in that way. Your comment about the relative compatibility/incompatibility of the systems is contradicted later in the exact same post when you say:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076095#post1076095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wish to convert the Tomb of Horrors from AD&amp;D 1.0 to Pathfinder - everything has a level rating, a difficulty rating, a direct correlation to a named spell, a named monster, a listing in the equipment tables, etc. I could do this in a day or so without much interruption. If I wish to convert the Keep on the Borderlands to Pathfinder - the materials transfer over by level, item name, monster name, etc. and can be formatted by challenge rating. WoD to CoD lacks that correlation. They were made separate games and the result is either play the new one and lose the value of everything you already had or play the old one and ignore the new materials.</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>I stated in the portion you quote the specific data and mechanics that make the conversion easier for converting chunks of Greyhawk to Pathfinder. There is no equivalent for converting anything except characters from WoD to CoD. The materials, the campaigns, the two opposed metas, prevent their interchangeability. As I indicated, it is either play the old one or play the new one. To combine them requires a massive amount of work which should not be necessary. They should not have made the CoD system to exclude and prevent the previous materials from being interactive. I still resent this action, and will do so until it is corrected - no matter how much I appreciate other aspects of the art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yet you then claim that they're irreconcilable. </div> </div> </div>They are. Because of the deliberate opposition of the meta of the two games. The mechanics did not need to be made antithetical - but because of the bias against the meta of the classical WoD they were woven into a new meta that was deliberately irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you're describing is actually fairly close to the emerging design philosophy of 5th edition D&amp;D. A reaction against supplement glut, a focus on core mechanics that are expanded and updated piecemeal via free material available online. I'd recommend checking it out. </div> </div> </div>I only play D&amp;D of any kind, including Pathfinder, because no one I am friends with is playing ST. D&amp;D, no matter what version, is a rigid mechanistic celebration of conceptual limitation inculcating the values of gluttony and avarice as substitutions for character development. I tolerate it in the same way a man tolerates the crass friends of an obnoxious in-law because his wife says so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately supplements that are all fluff and no crunch tend not to sell very well. Gamers gonna game. I certainly understand the desire to make plug and play easier for people who don't have a lot of time for game prep or homebrew. I think that's a big reason why adventure modules seem to be doing well lately. </div> </div> </div>On this we agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:34:24-07:00","id":1076331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076316#post1076316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only play D&amp;D of any kind, including Pathfinder, because no one I am friends with is playing ST. D&amp;D, no matter what version, is a rigid mechanistic celebration of conceptual limitation inculcating the values of gluttony and avarice as substitutions for character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, aren't you vociferous, using all this sesquipedalian terminology.<br /> <br /> I play and lead both WoD and DnD games, and I enjoy both immensely. Maybe the way your group plays can be summed up as crunchy loot-mongering, but that style isn't mandated by the system; my own games are certainly not oriented that way. Hell, last week, our group's halfling just gave up his prize magic sword in order to restore the honor of a local noble family.<br /> <br /> And if you haven't experienced 5e, I would suggest giving it a gander. It is sleek and fun. I am running Hoard of the Dragon Queen for two groups right now and we are having a blast. If this new edition of the WoD proves similar, I will be quite happy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> if they start making new adventures, or even updated old ones for WoD, I would pick them up, you bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:38:19-07:00","id":1076334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076316#post1076316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context. The person to whom I responded had just described the gaming community as a collection of seemingly flighty skittering birds jumping from feeder to feeder convinced that just over there the seeds will be different. In the hand a blade cast in bronze and a blade cast in steel may seem very different, but it is still only a blade. Exploring the human condition by acting out morality plays has existed since the ritual telling of the Ramayana began in the Treta Yuga. Rolling dice as a form of gaming has existed since before 3,000 BCE using hexahedrons made from sheep bones. Tetrahedrons going back before 2,600 BCE were used in games which re-enacted the battle between the imposed order of the gods against the primordial chaos from which the world was made in which the journey of man from life to death is fraught with obstacles, traps, and fortunes which propel us quickly along the path. Every video game is just an elaborately decorated version of Pong.<br /> Nihil nova sub soli. Ex barbariae e duc eos.<br /> Nothing new under the Sun. From Barbarism to lead them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that wasn't what was being said. You keep dunking all your statements in this slurring stream of reference that washes away their coherency and leaves them soaked in verbiage that isn't doing any work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a collector those hard copies that have never been opened may have some value. For gaming, the meta was made incompatible with the new supposedly meta-free set of rules which were never meta-free. Werewolf is specifically antithetical to the original meta. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in that statement indicates how value is supposedly destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I was a child they created child proof caps. My father would take me to the art classes he taught in continuing education. One night when the law required all things that might be poisonous in some way to have child proof caps, his students \u2013 mostly elderly people with arthritis, could not open their oil paints. Neither of course could my father, since they were child proof and he was an adult. So he handed it too me to open, and I did. The lady said, &quot;My how smart you are to be able to do this.&quot; To which I replied, &quot;Not really. It's just that children have all the time in the world to work on something and adults have too many things to do.&quot; Perhaps if you had been busy working in a coal mine or operating an automated loom like some urchin in the late 1800's you would have a better perspective of how our children may indulge themselves when not faced with the frivolous pursuits of paying bills, repairing the home, maintaining the car, buying and preparing food, etc. </div> </div> </div>Yet seventeen years later as an adult with a full time job, student loans, house chores, and health insurance I still have the time and the ability to do this. Because its really not that complicated. People make system hacks way harder than they need to be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I stated in the portion you quote the specific data and mechanics that make the conversion easier for converting chunks of Greyhawk to Pathfinder. There is no equivalent for converting anything except characters from WoD to CoD. The materials, the campaigns, the two opposed metas, prevent their interchangeability. As I indicated, it is either play the old one or play the new one. To combine them requires a massive amount of work which should not be necessary. They should not have made the CoD system to exclude and prevent the previous materials from being interactive. I still resent this action, and will do so until it is corrected - no matter how much I appreciate other aspects of the art. </div> </div> </div>Yet you stated that your 1st edition material was categorically incompatible with 2nd edition in the same post where you indicate that it isn't. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are. Because of the deliberate opposition of the meta of the two games. The mechanics did not need to be made antithetical - but because of the bias against the meta of the classical WoD they were woven into a new meta that was deliberately irreconcilable. </div> </div> </div>You seem to be operating under the belief that the CofD mechanics were designed to somehow prevent their use with WoD material. The fact that they were designed to support one set of games and not the set of games you wanted them to isn't the same thing as intentionally excluding them. You claim to like the CofD mechanics but not the meta and want to be able to port the WoD meta into the CofD mechanics. You can certainly give it a try, I've done it, but I'm not sure its going to turn out the way you want it. You can't actually bend the CofD mechanics perfectly around the WoD because they're designed to do something that <i>isn't that.</i> At some level you either have to sacrifice some aspect of the CofD mechanics or the WoD meta. That's not a fault of design though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I only play D&amp;D of any kind, including Pathfinder, because no one I am friends with is playing ST. D&amp;D, no matter what version, is a rigid mechanistic celebration of conceptual limitation inculcating the values of gluttony and avarice as substitutions for character development. I tolerate it in the same way a man tolerates the crass friends of an obnoxious in-law because his wife says so. </div> </div> </div>Whatever floats your boat I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:58:00-07:00","id":1076345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076331#post1076331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I play and lead both WoD and DnD games, and I enjoy both immensely. Maybe the way your group plays can be summed up as crunchy loot-mongering, but that style isn't mandated by the system; my own games are certainly not oriented that way. Hell, last week, our group's halfling just gave up his prize magic sword in order to restore the honor of a local noble family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck my group mostly uses 3.5 as a vehicle for weird settings that plumb conceptual underpinnings of different genres, explore mechanical implications if taken to logical extremes and their impact on the game world, or just pet projects in academic theory. 3.5's sometimes obtuse crunchiness and sheer level of supplement glut make it weirdly ideal for these purposes.<br /> <br /> Games are what you make them. Because they're games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:44:00-07:00","id":1076356,"title":"","content":"As an instructor of Literature and Rhetoric, I would give this a B- for undergraduate work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:07:53-07:00","id":1076714,"title":"","content":"This is... very very wordy. To the point where it's actively painful to attempt to extract meaning. And I have to deal with gerglish tech manuals on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> My general answer is: Before demanding or discussing the impact of a fifth edition, let's see how WWP does with the 4th edition they're in the midst of writing first, eh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:22:43-07:00","id":1076724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076714#post1076714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general answer is: Before demanding or discussing the impact of a fifth edition, let's see how WWP does with the 4th edition they're in the midst of writing first, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>5th edition is what they're writing for. Apparently, WoD 20th Anniversary is considered to be WoD4e in their eyes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:08:11-07:00","id":1076734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076724#post1076724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5th edition is what they're writing for. Apparently, WoD 20th Anniversary is considered to be WoD4e in their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually agreeing with them. Revised wasn't named &quot;3rd edition&quot;, it was Revised, but it was the 3rd edition of the game. The 20ths are named X20th, but they are new editions and did increasingly bigger changes to the rules from Vampire to Mage, so they're indeed the 4th iterations of the games. At least the games which made it through all editions and then my head starts hurting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:21:25-07:00","id":1076736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076331#post1076331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, aren't you vociferous, using all this sesquipedalian terminology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't apologize for growing up in a family of artists, librarians, and teachers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the way your group plays can be summed up as crunchy loot-mongering </div> </div> </div>The mechanics of the system apply development solely from crunchy loot and slaughter addiction. Video game on paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:23:18-07:00","id":1076737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076356#post1076356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an instructor of Literature and Rhetoric, I would give this a B- for undergraduate work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I detest Hemingway and his destruction of the American Intellect. But I recognize there are those who feel simplicity is superior to prose. Frankly, your posit is meaningless to my life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:50:26-07:00","id":1076744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't apologize for growing up in a family of artists, librarians, and teachers.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> The mechanics of the system apply development solely from crunchy loot and slaughter addiction. Video game on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... you're smart enough to vomit out these overwrought borderline word salad diatribes, but you can't quite figure out how to make DnD be anything but a slaughterfest.<br /> <br /> Alright. Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-12-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T18:57:04-07:00","id":1076747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076334#post1076334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that wasn't what was being said.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wasn't expressly stated, it was implied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in this slurring stream of reference that washes away their coherency and leaves them soaked in verbiage that isn't doing any work. </div> </div> </div>I am not responsible for a faulty receiver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing in that statement indicates how value is supposedly destroyed. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it did. Any intuitive thinker would see this. Since you cannot apparently perceive this way, you will be fundamentally incapable of understanding my statement to that degree of difference in perception. Since this is likely as much a focus of experience as hard wiring, it is merely a difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People make system hacks way harder than they need to be. </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between a rapier and a nuclear weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yet you stated that your 1st edition material was categorically incompatible with 2nd edition in the same post where you indicate that it isn't. </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. From a sensorial approach perhaps, but not from a conceptual one. Following the implications and behavior of the system mechanics. They are anathema to one another because the second is designed to be counter-intuitive to the meta of the first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that they were designed to support one set of games and not the set of games you wanted them to isn't the same thing as intentionally excluding them. </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. It is precisely because the choice was made specifically to oppose the previous meta that it does. It is an observable and deliberate choice. Gifts do not directly convert because the renown system is different. Difficulties designed and adapted to playtesting involving a higher degree of botches have no conversion for the static difficulty of the new system. Limitations in the newer rules to justifiably avoid the Epic OP that occurred in the previous meta, such as Samual Haight and Zubeida, were choices that inherently change the intuitive structure and make the metas of the rules incompatible. You acknowledge this when you state:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't actually bend the CofD mechanics perfectly around the WoD because they're designed to do something that <i>isn't that.</i> At some level you either have to sacrifice some aspect of the CofD mechanics or the WoD meta. That's not a fault of design though. </div> </div> </div>To be a fault, it would have to be a defect of physical implication, a weakness of character, or a mistake. It was none of these. It was a specific choice to make the systems opposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:46:08-07:00","id":1076785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076747#post1076747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it wasn't expressly stated, it was implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you read an implication into the argument presented and chose to argue against that rather than the actual position of the person you were debating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not responsible for a faulty receiver. </div> </div> </div>I get being verbose. I enjoy a deep well of reference as much as the next guy, and I'm more than capable of being a pretentious thesaurus. Your prose is so meandering though that it makes extracting a thesis difficult. When your words become an obstacle to your meaning they aren't doing any work. I used to have a very similar writing style, but a pair of professors in college were able to impress on me the value of structure, precision, and brevity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it did. Any intuitive thinker would see this. Since you cannot apparently perceive this way, you will be fundamentally incapable of understanding my statement to that degree of difference in perception. Since this is likely as much a focus of experience as hard wiring, it is merely a difference. </div> </div> </div>I <i>am</i> actually an &quot;intuitive&quot; thinker. That entire model of cognition and personality has about as much rigor as zodiac signs, but even if we pretend that its a useful distinction your premise is faulty because at least one intuitive thinker clearly isn't seeing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a difference between a rapier and a nuclear weapon. </div> </div> </div>A factual statement, but once again one that doesn't actually say anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incorrect. From a sensorial approach perhaps, but not from a conceptual one. Following the implications and behavior of the system mechanics. They are anathema to one another because the second is designed to be counter-intuitive to the meta of the first. </div> </div> </div>Except that, again, you mention how simply you can convert 1st edition to Pathfinder if you wanted to but apparently 1st to 2nd is too tall of an order. Also, what &quot;meta&quot; exists in early AD&amp;D?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is incorrect. It is precisely because the choice was made specifically to oppose the previous meta that it does. It is an observable and deliberate choice. Gifts do not directly convert because the renown system is different. Difficulties designed and adapted to playtesting involving a higher degree of botches have no conversion for the static difficulty of the new system. Limitations in the newer rules to justifiably avoid the Epic OP that occurred in the previous meta, such as Samual Haight and Zubeida, were choices that inherently change the intuitive structure and make the metas of the rules incompatible. </div> </div> </div>So we're back to you liking CofD because its better but not liking it because its different. Glad we've been able to make so much progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 04-11-2017, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T21:09:52-07:00","id":1076795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076736#post1076736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics of the system apply development solely from crunchy loot and slaughter addiction. Video game on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even 1st edition AD&amp;D allows for gaining XP from &quot;solving or overcoming problems through professional means.&quot; It still has the whole gold-is-experience thing, but that's so easy to handwave it doesn't even require a hack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T21:49:42-07:00","id":1076805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076737#post1076737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I detest Hemingway and his destruction of the American Intellect. But I recognize there are those who feel simplicity is superior to prose. Frankly, your posit is meaningless to my life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your opinions on Hemingway are immaterial; your opinions on some sort of &quot;American Intellect&quot; even more so. Frankly, your<b> thesis is muddled</b>, your<b> writing is meandering</b> and <b>unfocused</b>, and your <b>evidence is anecdotal</b>, <i>at best</i>. As in exercise in critical thought, it fails. Be glad I don't ask for an annotated bibliography.<br /> <br /> As you posted this in a public internet forum designed to encourage discussion, it could reasonably be assumed you desired some sort of feedback, but your passive-aggressive denials and recriminations to any and all perceived critique has shown that you only really wanted Reddit-esque &quot;likes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just because you read Kierkegaard on your own and have access to a thesaurus doesn't make you part of the literati.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:55:05-07:00","id":1076833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076734#post1076734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the games which made it through all editions and then my head starts hurting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...oh yeah:<br /> <br /> -Wraith20 and Changeling20 are technically their third editions since they never made it to Revised.<br /> -A theoretical Hunter20, Mummy20, and Demon20 would be their second edition since they first popped up during the Revised era AKA the tail end (at the time) of WoD.<br /> <br /> Yeah I think I'll just stick to calling them &quot;20th Anniversary Editions&quot;. Much easier that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:06:51-07:00","id":1077114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076833#post1076833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...oh yeah:<br /> <br /> -Wraith20 and Changeling20 are technically their third editions since they never made it to Revised.<br /> -A theoretical Hunter20, Mummy20, and Demon20 would be their second edition since they first popped up during the Revised era AKA the tail end (at the time) of WoD.<br /> <br /> Yeah I think I'll just stick to calling them &quot;20th Anniversary Editions&quot;. Much easier that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, what would you call the new editions after the 20ths to not confuse new and existing fans (they are already confused with the whole NWoD/CofD/WoD/20th thing)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:23:07-07:00","id":1077165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077114#post1077114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, what would you call the new editions after the 20ths to not confuse new and existing fans (they are already confused with the whole NWoD/CofD/WoD/20th thing)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a no-win scenario, honestly.<br /> <br /> When they come out, I'll probably just call them 5th Editions, even if nu-WW decides not to call them that. Even then, that'll create confusion for new and/or lapsed fans that are curious about the previous editions.<br /> <br /> Certainly I'm not looking forward to the conversation I might have for a new player asking why the can't seem to find Changeling 3rd and/or 4th edition but can find a 1st, 2nd, and 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-12-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:27:17-07:00","id":1077274,"title":"","content":"The twenty-first edition? Just to keep things uniform?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:54:07-07:00","id":1077338,"title":"","content":"Well since they plan on lumping them all in under the setting of &quot;one world of darkness&quot; I refer to them as 1wod.<br /> <br /> The anniversary editors I call X20 with X being the splat type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:07:00-07:00","id":1077373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077274#post1077274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The twenty-first edition? Just to keep things uniform?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...<br /> <br /> It's not 2012 anymore for Vampire. Or 2013 for Werewolf. Or 2014 for Mage, etc.<br /> <br /> So nah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:19:27-07:00","id":1077426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077165#post1077165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a no-win scenario, honestly.<br /> <br /> When they come out, I'll probably just call them 5th Editions, even if nu-WW decides not to call them that. Even then, that'll create confusion for new and/or lapsed fans that are curious about the previous editions.<br /> <br /> Certainly I'm not looking forward to the conversation I might have for a new player asking why the can't seem to find Changeling 3rd and/or 4th edition but can find a 1st, 2nd, and 5th edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think it'd be fairly easy. Edition refers to the core rules of the system and setting, and is applied across the board to all lines weather they received their own book that edition or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:58:12-07:00","id":1077451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076785#post1076785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you read an implication into the argument presented and chose to argue against that rather than the actual position of the person you were debating.</div> </div> </div> </div> The implication was fundamental to the posit. Without it the posit had no foundation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> were able to impress on me the value of structure, precision, and brevity. </div> </div> </div>The dumbing down of the American Mind. It began with Hemingway and everything he has influenced is corrupted toward imbecility - to have no foundation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>am</i> actually an &quot;intuitive&quot; thinker. That entire model of cognition and personality has about as much rigor as zodiac signs, but even if we pretend that its a useful distinction your premise is faulty because at least one intuitive thinker clearly isn't seeing it. </div> </div> </div> If that were true you would not be limiting your analysis to sensual perception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A factual statement, but once again one that doesn't actually say anything. </div> </div> </div>By nature all factual statements say a fact. It also has contextual meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that, again, you mention how simply you can convert 1st edition to Pathfinder if you wanted to but apparently 1st to 2nd is too tall of an order. Also, what &quot;meta&quot; exists in early AD&amp;D? </div> </div> </div>You aren't paying attention. I discussed the sections of the mechanics in 3.5 E (hence also Pathfinder) for conversion. Like most of what I state you ignore what you find inconvenient. This is not because of my writing style it is willful inattention to detail. Challenge Rating, the conversion of the spells to the new mechanics each time the game is updated, the mechanics for determining level appropriate encounters (so that every 13 appropriate encounters equals a level of character advancement), etc. make converting a dungeon like Keep on the Borderlands a plug and play transition. This is not true going between VtM and VtR, MtA and MtAw, WtA and WtF, WtO and GtSE, CtD and CtL, etc. The powers were not converted and the Meta of the second set was created deliberately to be antithetical to the first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we're back to you liking CofD because its better but not liking it because its different. Glad we've been able to make so much progress. </div> </div> </div>No we aren't. Because you failed or refused to observe the posit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:09:52-07:00","id":1077460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1076805#post1076805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you read Kierkegaard on your own and have access to a thesaurus doesn't make you part of the literati.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had a professor here in a town 0.38 square miles which insisted that if people had chickens and the chickens laid eggs that all the people in town would get sick and die. She knew this because she was a professor who taught about managing in the hotel industry.<br /> <br /> I haven't quoted Kierkegaard. And I only use a thesaurus when I wish to avoid using a word twice in the same paragraph or sentence for the same meaning.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the difference between Critical Thoughts and Critical Thinking hasn't occurred to you yet.<br /> <br /> As for my opinion concerning the effect of Hemingway on American illiteracy, having been raised almost exclusively on the literature of the real English, I have a control group to compare against. And you can either accept that Hemingway's deliberate dumbing down of daily literature is responsible for the outcome or that all of you who chose to be teachers are collectively at fault. I am affording you the benefit of the doubt. Your choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:13:11-07:00","id":1077465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077165#post1077165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly I'm not looking forward to the conversation I might have for a new player asking why the can't seem to find Changeling 3rd and/or 4th edition but can find a 1st, 2nd, and 5th edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abandon the computer lingo of 1.0, 2.0, 5.0, etc. and go with year or decade of the zeitgeist described in the publication. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:44:32-07:00","id":1077482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077465#post1077465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abandon the computer lingo of 1.0, 2.0, 5.0, etc. and go with year or decade of the zeitgeist described in the publication. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Only do that for reboot movies.<br /> <br /> And what 1.0 and 2.0? You said that, not me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:50:47-07:00","id":1077484,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain OP's argument or problem in the language an American blue collar factory worker would understand? Because all I'm getting so far is that something is wrong but they don't have a solution to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-13-2017, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:08:15-07:00","id":1077495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077451#post1077451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The implication was fundamental to the posit. Without it the posit had no foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;posit&quot; was that new editions emerged over time because of developments and experiments in game design. The implication you read into it (I think, you're not super clear) was that people refuse to play old things and will always chase the shiny new thing because they're idiots. So you responded by saying that there were no new concepts and the differences we perceived between them were a product of immaturity. In addition to that implication being not particularly related to the position being offered, you also don't really address that implication. I don't even know <i>what</i> you're addressing anymore because all you ever seem to offer is a sloshing mess of contradictions and poor attempts at pedantry. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dumbing down of the American Mind. It began with Hemingway and everything he has influenced is corrupted toward imbecility - to have no foundation. </div> </div> </div>Cool story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that were true you would not be limiting your analysis to sensual perception. </div> </div> </div>And no true Scotsman puts sugar on his porridge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By nature all factual statements say a fact. It also has contextual meaning. </div> </div> </div>How nice of you to clarify what that contextual meaning was supposed to be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You aren't paying attention. I discussed the sections of the mechanics in 3.5 E (hence also Pathfinder) for conversion. Like most of what I state you ignore what you find inconvenient. This is not because of my writing style it is willful inattention to detail. Challenge Rating, the conversion of the spells to the new mechanics each time the game is updated, the mechanics for determining level appropriate encounters (so that every 13 appropriate encounters equals a level of character advancement), etc. make converting a dungeon like Keep on the Borderlands a plug and play transition. This is not true going between VtM and VtR, MtA and MtAw, WtA and WtF, WtO and GtSE, CtD and CtL, etc. The powers were not converted and the Meta of the second set was created deliberately to be antithetical to the first. </div> </div> </div>You aren't paying attention. That thought was specifically in relation to your assertions about conversions and compatibility in D&amp;D because they formed a cornerstone of your objection to new game editions. The debate about CofD vs WoD was broken off into a separate thought, which you responded to with...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No we aren't. Because you failed or refused to observe the posit. </div> </div> </div>...something that is not a sentence. Anyway, we're done here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T23:15:05-07:00","id":1077539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077460#post1077460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had a professor here in a town 0.38 square miles which insisted that if people had chickens and the chickens laid eggs that all the people in town would get sick and die. She knew this because she was a professor who taught about managing in the hotel industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your anecdotes are just that - anecdotal, and therefore worthless to the discussion at hand.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't quoted Kierkegaard. And I only use a thesaurus when I wish to avoid using a word twice in the same paragraph or sentence for the same meaning. </div> </div> </div>It's a shame that for all those dime-store words, hyperbole is lost on you.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps the difference between Critical Thoughts and Critical Thinking hasn't occurred to you yet. </div> </div> </div>Critical <u><i>thinking</i></u> leads to critical <u><i>thought</i></u>, something which you have spectacularly failed to demonstrate here. You are neither as objective nor removed as you desire to be. And to round it all out (emphasis mine):<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for my opinion concerning the effect of Hemingway on American illiteracy, having been raised almost exclusively on the literature of the<b> real English</b>, I have a control group to compare against. And you can either accept that Hemingway's deliberate dumbing down of daily literature is responsible for the outcome or that all of you who chose to be teachers are collectively at fault. I am affording you the benefit of the doubt. Your choice. </div> </div> </div>Full disclosure: I don't even particularly <i>like</i> Hemingway, but laying some form of &quot;fault&quot; or &quot;blame&quot; at the feet of a singular author <b>belies a fundamental misunderstanding of Modernist Literature</b>, and Literature as a whole.<br /> <br /> You're a critic with no credentials, and being contrarian solely for the sake of being combative is only rewarded with a $5 Hot Topic gift card<sup>1</sup> around here.<br /> <br /> You like your anecdotes, so here's one for you: &quot;A little learning is a dangerous thing&quot; - the magniloquence of your writing reveals the pretense of your erudition; the attempts to bamboozle<sup>2</sup> the uninitiated fall flat when faced by knowledgeable sources (to hijack your turns of phrase).<br /> <br /> I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> - we're done here. You've uncloaked yourself to be either a troll, which is willfully malevolent, or worse (and sadly) - simply maliciously obtuse.<br /> <br /> <sup>1 Gift card may or may not be expired.<br /> 2 What a great word.</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:48:08-07:00","id":1077559,"title":"","content":"Since we're kinda done here and all, clarification on my own point from the other thread:<br /> <br /> I also posited that as game design is expanded and refined, that new editions are more appealing to the customer base for RPGs. But that's because new editions represent refinements that incorporate expanded - either through innovation or experimentation - design concepts. Not every new edition succeeds, but in aggregate they trend towards overall game play experience improvement by virtue of better designs learned from all the decades of RPGs being made.<br /> <br /> The whole point is to push back against the idea of a mechanically static RPG that would last for generations of players is tenable (not even getting into the matter of preference that is if getting to that product is desirable). That a game that tries to avoid mechanical overhauls is inevitably (at least with the current state of RPG design having not yet fully explored all the boundaries of what RPGs are capable of, since games are still coming out with unique iterations of old ideas let alone new ones) bound towards abandonment.<br /> <br /> Not because of any fickleness on the behalf of the customers, but simply because better games born from expansion and refinement would supplant the old ones. Like so many other things, there will always been people that like the classic icons for that status, and some even to the point of rejecting anything but a classic. Classic cars can be marvelous pieces of artistic expression, and incredibly visceral fun to drive, but we didn't stop making cars after a collection of classic designs were made. We keep making newer and better cars, even if a lot of them are boring samey cars. Even with all the old classics, we also manage to make new classics every few years too.<br /> <br /> Likewise, RPGs have their classic iconic games that people still play after decades, but as RPG design evolves and improves game play experience, newer systems are the ones that sell the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:20:43-07:00","id":1077713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077539#post1077539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your anecdotes are just that - anecdotal, and therefore worthless</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure that is what you said to Aesop when he asked you to Waltz amidst the singing flowers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're a critic with no credentials </div> </div> </div>So, I see you feel elections should be abolished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A little learning is a dangerous thing </div> </div> </div>Which is why I not only drank, but bathed in the Pierian Spring.<br /> <br /> Hemingway created a form of writing based on never using words above a 5th grade reading level and debasing sentences to a simple subject and simple predicate. He did this to enhance his position at the Kansas City Star by creating more room for commercial advertizing space. The writing of the late 1800's is by far superior because it was not meant to debase itself and to limit the exposure of the public mind to the verbage of children. You may not like his stories, but you support his corruption of the language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:24:13-07:00","id":1077715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077482#post1077482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Only do that for reboot movies.<br /> <br /> And what 1.0 and 2.0? You said that, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edition 1 or edition 1.0, Edition 3 or Edition 3.5. The slang applied in other games is influencing the perception of this one. I was suggesting we go against the Trend. Use Edition 1990 vs. Edition 2000, or 2010. Lump them by a decade or group of years used for publication.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:33:55-07:00","id":1077720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077495#post1077495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to that implication being not particularly related to the position being offered, you also don't really address that implication. I don't even know <i>what</i> you're addressing anymore because all you ever seem to offer is a sloshing mess of contradictions and poor attempts at pedantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't a need to address it further. Hence, the declaration of other ideas and concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How nice of you to clarify what that contextual meaning was supposed to be. </div> </div> </div>There should be no need for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You aren't paying attention. That thought was specifically in relation to your assertions about conversions and compatibility in D&amp;D because they formed a cornerstone of your objection to new game editions. The debate about CofD vs WoD was broken off into a separate thought, which you responded to with... </div> </div> </div>You still fail or refuse to observe the posit. P:Q::M:N. Nor is your assessment of gramar correct. But that is the fault of an education system directed by liberals who abandoned good English decades ago while they were tripping at Woodstock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, we're done here. </div> </div> </div>Good-bye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T08:19:10-07:00","id":1077747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1075873-\u200bcritical-thoughts-on-the-potential-in-a-5th-edition-of-the-game?p=1077559#post1077559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also posited that as game design is expanded and refined, that new editions are more appealing to the customer base for RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>And admitted that it was not a new edition of the game but a new game separate and distinct with no connection to or intended interaction with the previous game. Making the previous game an abandoned, no longer supported, concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole point is [that] push back against the idea of a mechanically static RPG that would last for generations of players is tenable (not even getting into the matter of preference that is if getting to that product is desirable). That a game that tries to avoid mechanical overhauls is inevitably bound towards abandonment. At least with the current state of RPG design having not yet fully explored all the boundaries of what RPGs are capable of, since games are still coming out with unique iterations of old ideas let alone new ones. </div> </div> </div>While the transformation of the Tachi into Katana took millennia, the steel of the west varied so much that one might even say the Tsimisce had infected it with vicissitude. In the West, perhaps inevitably so, it is the trend to screech against the form of steel, shadow boxing it from within its tempered boundaries. In the east, alterations to the blade were slow, methodical, and made blades usable for generations with emphasis on improving the wielder and not the already carefully perfected wielded. In the US, Anno Mundi is 1776 and in Canada it is a slow birth crowning the cannal of the Fairy Queendom in 1867 and finally being free enough to swaddle at their Anno Mundi of 1982. The thoughtful child learns first how to learn. Such a child attends school, not to learn, but expresses self mastery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not because of any fickleness on the behalf of the customers, but simply because better games born from expansion and refinement would supplant the old ones. Like so many other things, there will always been people that like the classic icons for that status, and some even to the point of rejecting anything but a classic. Classic cars can be marvelous pieces of artistic expression, and incredibly visceral fun to drive, but we didn't stop making cars after a collection of classic designs were made. We keep making newer and better cars, even if a lot of them are boring samey cars. Even with all the old classics, we also manage to make new classics every few years too. </div> </div> </div>And yet, any physicist of the late 1800s could have told you that when you design all vehicles in a wind tunnel they will ultimately all start to look like half of a flattened egg.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, RPGs have their classic iconic games that people still play after decades, but as RPG design evolves and improves game play experience, newer systems are the ones that sell the best. </div> </div> </div>Because of course, the old thing belongs in the hospice to be wherehoused until dead. That is the usual value of youth in a young country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:42:45-07:00","id":1077892,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">OK, I've seen enough. Whithers if you can't communicate clearly and succinctly without throwing barbs at other users then find another forum to frequent. You've been intentionally goading other users to violate forum rules and have been violating those rules yourself. This is the only warning you will get, stop the offending behavior or I will ban you from these forums. <br /> <br /> \u200bTo the users that have responded to insult with insult you are also being warned. Taking the bait and responding with posts that are rules violations still makes you guilty of violating forum rules and this is not acceptable. Don't make the mod staff have to take action, we don't enjoy it and you can avoid that by simply not responding to the provocation. Flag the offending post and move on.<br /> <br /> This thread is being closed. If I see the behavior that got this thread closed continued elsewhere suspensions will be given out.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}